Subject: Shapes that compiled tables key by address are marked observed, and only their frees move an epoch

What this does
  - `JSShape.aot_observed` is a real field (it was a counters-only field): set when a PIC cell holds the shape and when `qjs_aot_shape_slot` / `qjs_aot_shape_method` read it. `JSRuntime.shape_obs_epoch`, right after `shape_free_epoch`, moves when an observed shape is freed or edited in place (and at the three places that move a shape allocation).

Why we need it
  The switch arms' slot tables and the learned method tables keep shapes by address without a reference. They validated against `shape_free_epoch`, which moves whenever ANY shape is freed: 40,000 times per deltablue unit, almost all of them the throwaway shape every `new Array()` builds and frees. Each move made every arm and every method table refill (~18 Minsn per unit). A table now validates against `shape_obs_epoch`, which the churn of unobserved shapes does not touch.

Soundness
  A table only keeps shapes it passed to `qjs_aot_shape_slot` / `qjs_aot_shape_method`, and those set the bit before the table stores the address, so freeing or editing a kept shape always moves `shape_obs_epoch`. Other users of `shape_free_epoch` (constructor-wrapper cache, constructor caches, the global stub cache) are unchanged.

Functions touched
  `js_new_shape2`, `js_free_shape0`, `resize_properties`, `compact_properties`, `add_property`, `js_shape_prepare_update`, the PIC fill, `qjs_aot_shape_slot`, `qjs_aot_shape_method`, `js_aot_gen_layout` (static assertion).

No.

